# Runtime image build context. The Dockerfile COPYs only `app/` (production); the test
# stage mounts the source at run instead of baking it. Exclude everything that must never
# enter an image or would bust the build cache.

# Git, at every depth
**/.git
.gitignore

# Python / caches. Bytecode is excluded at EVERY depth: a bare pattern matches only at the
# context root, so `__pycache__` alone would let app/**/__pycache__ into the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.so
.Python
.venv
venv/
env/
ENV/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Secrets, env files, credentials and keys must NEVER enter the image, at ANY depth: a bare
# `.env.*` matches only at the context root, so a gitignored app/.env.local would ship inside
# app/. Only the committed .env.example template is re-included.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!.env.example
**/*credentials.json
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
# Editor backups beside source (app/config.py~ would ship a stale copy of the code)
**/*~

# Runtime output + quarantined legacy files (bind-mounted / local-only, never baked)
**/output/
**/export/
src/

# Docs / dashboards (not needed in the runtime image)
docs/
grafana/
*.md

# Compose / Dockerfiles / build tooling
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
Makefile

# OS / editor
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude
.claude/
